@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Liferay University Passport Access Sandbox
	Testing the Liferay University Passport Access portlet on sandbox.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the contact entitlement definitions on koroneiki with the following name values
	| Liferay Role |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| Digital Enterprise Production  |
	| Portal Production              |
	| Enterprise Search - Production |
	| Platinum Subscription          |
	| Gold Subscription              |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Platinum Subscription |
	| Gold Subscription     |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Role  |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORONEKORONE |
	* I tear down the sandbox users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I tear down the sandbox users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	| osb.koroneiki4@liferay.com.broken    |
	| osb.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki3@lrpartner.com.broken  |
	* I tear down the sandbox organizations with the following names from customer.liferay.com
	| Koroneiki Liferay Role |

Scenario: Request passport access as dxp customers
	New passports should be able to be requested by dxp customers.

	Given I create a sandbox user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a sandbox user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a koroneiki user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Digital Enterprise Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Platinum Subscription | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with a koroneiki uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                      |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Digital Enterprise Production" and contact role with the name "Liferay Account Role" and type "Account Customer" with the following values
	| Description | Liferay Role Entitlement |
	| Name        | Liferay Role             |
	| Status      | Approved                 |
	And I create a support sandbox organization with the name "Koroneiki Liferay Role"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Role"
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I update the sandbox support password for user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the sandbox support password for user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Guest"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Guest"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support organization "Customer"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support organization "Customer"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support organization "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support organization "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Verified User"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Verified User"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I assign the sandbox support user with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I log into the support homepage as "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser" on the sandbox
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page on the sandbox
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form on the sandbox
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| End User Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	| Company Name           | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| End User Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser" on the sandbox
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page on the sandbox
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form on the sandbox
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| End User Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	| Company Name           | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| End User Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |

